BEGIN <TICKET-SUMMARY>
[B1280-6] Browser rows in web/e2e/mock-rows.spec.ts: frame() sleeps a fixed 500 ms for 18 of its 19 calls and only the dashboard row waits for its data; reopened after pull request 286 (Minor, test-only)
END <TICKET-SUMMARY>
BEGIN <TICKET-DESCRIPTION>
BLUF: the browser rows in web/e2e/mock-rows.spec.ts end their page set-up with a fixed half-second sleep, page.waitForTimeout(500), for 18 of the 19 calls of the frame() helper; only the dashboard row waits for the page's data. It changes no product behaviour, no user sees a defect behind it, and nothing here is deployed. This is finding B1280-6 of gate B1280, reopened: the file that landed holds the sleeps again.
Finding B1280-6, reopened (Minor by the gate's grading; test-only): at main <<MAIN-SHA8>> the helper frame() (web/e2e/mock-rows.spec.ts line 19) ends with await page.waitForTimeout(500); at line 26 unless the caller passes a dataReady function (line 25). Of the 19 calls of frame(), one, at line 80, passes a data function (dashboardData); the other 18, at lines <<CALL-LINES>>, take the sleep. It is the file's only waitForTimeout (read at main <<MAIN-SHA8>> on <<READ-DATE>> by program; the file has <<FILE-LINES>> lines).
How it came back: gate B1289 (round 2, the cap) found the replacement wait did not wait for the page's data (B1289 line 14); the builder then restored round 1's version of the file (B1291 line 65) and added a data wait for the dashboard row only (B1298 line 52). The builder's notes say the other rows still pause 500 ms and were not re-measured (B1291 line 55, B1298 line 106). Pull request 286 landed in that state (squash 73adb50c).
Evidence that the weakness is real (the gates', not re-run): with every data call of the page answered 300 ms late, the round-1 file read 3 of 9 red, only on /workspace, whose list needs more than one call; the replacement wait that did not wait for data read 9 of 9 red (B1289 line 74).
Fix shape, as the gates wrote it (B1280 line 162; B1289 line 14): wait on a condition the page shows, never on time: each page path named above gets its own data-ready wait, as the dashboard row already does (dashboardData, line 80); keep the optional argument of frame(); add no waitForTimeout, setTimeout, .only or .skip; pin properties, not one pixel figure.
Done when: no call of frame() in web/e2e/mock-rows.spec.ts reaches a fixed sleep, each of the 19 calls waiting on its own page's data or on a condition the page shows, with 0 new waitForTimeout, setTimeout, .only or .skip in the file, and the file's rows stay green when the page's data calls are answered 300 ms late (the instrument of B1289 line 74); or the item is recorded as accepted or declined; no product behaviour changes. The findings are the gates'; the records seat re-read the lines and did not re-run the gates' instruments. Provenance: gates B1280 (round 1 of 2, no go; finding B1280-6, 2026-11-04_B1280_STATUS.md line 162) and B1289 (round 2 of 2, no go at the cap; 2026-11-04_B1289_STATUS.md lines 1, 14 and 74), builder notes B1291 and B1298, all in 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/ of the analysis repository; pull request 286 (squash 73adb50c). Decision records: entries C-295, C-296 and C-301; backlog row B1310-1. Filed by records brief B1310, 2026-11-06. [REC-FILE-B1280-6-06NOV-B1310]
END <TICKET-DESCRIPTION>
(Six paragraphs, one per line of the description block: the BLUF, the finding, how it came back, the evidence, the fix shape, and the done-when with its provenance on the sixth line, as B1251 and B1256 did. `<<CALL-LINES>>` is the 18 line numbers of S2 joined by commas and "and", printed by program; `<<FILE-LINES>>` is the line count; `<<READ-DATE>>` is `2026-11-06`.)

